+  provider name and are NOT renamed at all, because they carry raw per-match stats rather than
+  metrics. What he was shown before answering: that `mart_player_match_log` and
+  `mart_player_fixture_stats` pass raw per-fixture numbers straight through; that this is the
+  `!111` precedent (team metric `goals_for` → `goals` LEFT `int_legs__team_match.goals_for` in
+  place, and "a metric and its column may legitimately differ"); and that it changes what a couple
+  of published mart columns are called. Applied: those marts plus `mart_team_fixture_stats`,
+  `int_legs__*`, `3_core`, `2_base` and `1_staging` are out of the edit set entirely. Measured, every
+  occurrence in them is a dotted read — so this ruling alone removes a whole class of round 1's
+  failures.
+
+  ⭐ **THE MISSING CHECK, BUILT AND WATCHED GOING RED.** A static resolver walks each model's
+  CTE/`ref()` chain and checks every dotted reference against the columns the relation declares:
+  **25 of 28 resolved and verified, 3 unresolved and REPORTED rather than skipped.** Reproducing the
+  round-1 defect turns it red with the exact diagnosis — "reads s.shots_player where s =
+  fct_fixture_player_stats, which does not emit 'shots_player'". It is a floor, not a ceiling:
+  static, 25 of 28, and `data:build:mr` remains the authority.
+  ⛔ **WHETHER IT SHOULD BECOME A COMMITTED CI GATE IS RAISED AND NOT TAKEN** — a new mechanism, and
+  therefore the CPO's/CTO's. Six batches remain with identical exposure.
+
+  ⚠ A CORRECTION TO THE PROGRAMME BLOCK, APPENDED NOT EDITED. Its 35-row table closes "UNCHANGED,
+  all 14: the 13 `_per90` names and `minutes_per_appearance`". The seed holds **48** player rows and
+  the list **35**, so the unchanged set is **13** — `key_passes_per90` is counted twice, being both a
+  `_per90` name and a rename-list entry (`key_passes_per90 → passes_key_per90`). True set: 12
+  `_per90` names + `minutes_per_appearance`. Verified both directions.
+
+  ⚠ AND A PROCESS MISTAKE OF MINE, raised by `analytics-engineer-reviewer`: I reverted the code while
+  reviewers were still reading, so one of them saw the working tree change under it mid-review. Its
+  findings came from the static patch and hold, but I gave it reason to doubt what it was seeing.
+  **Wait for every reviewer to return before touching the tree.**
+
+  ⭐ The 1604-description count is the CPO's earlier "re-point them" ruling measured again: identical
+  to the base, where blanking the borrowed references would have left 1592.
+
+  ⛔⛔ **ROUND 2 THEN FAILED 5–0 ON THE SAME DEFECT, AND THAT IS THE ENTRY WORTH KEEPING.** Two
+  instances, both real:
+    · `int_player_season__metrics.sql:45-46` — `sum(shots_total) as shots_player`, a BARE read of
+      `club_season` = `ref('int_player_club_season__metrics')`, a METRIC relation this same branch
+      renames. Found INDEPENDENTLY by `scope-auditor`, `analytics-engineer-reviewer`,
+      `football-analytics-expert-reviewer` and `platform-reviewer`.
+    · `docs/wireframes/03_player_profile.md:126` — prose naming `shots_player` in a line documenting
+      the matchstats payload, which comes from `mart_player_fixture_stats`: a provider surface that
+      does not rename under the "yes" ruling. Found by `bi-analyst-reviewer`.
+  ⭐⭐ **AND IT IS ONE MISTAKE, NOT FIVE SURFACES OF BAD LUCK. For dotted reads I asked the right
+  question — DOES THE SOURCE RELATION RENAME THIS COLUMN? For bare reads I asked a different one:
+  does the alias happen to match the inner name?** Those questions agree most of the time and
+  disagree exactly where it matters. Every instance across both rounds is that one inconsistency:
+  alias, dotted, bare, prose and seed are shapes, not rules. **THE RULE IS: A REFERENCE FOLLOWS ITS
+  SOURCE.** Shape only tells you what is being read.
+  ⚠ **MY OWN RESOLVER REPEATED THE MISTAKE IN MINIATURE**, and `platform-reviewer` named it: built
+  for DOTTED references only, it reported "25 of 28 resolved, 0 broken" while a model sat broken on a
+  bare read. **A check that gives false confidence is worse than no check** — the third instance of
+  that class in two days, after the vacuous `sed` intersection and the empty flagged-file list.
+  Extended to follow sources through CTE chains for both shapes: 31 checked, 0 broken, and it flags
+  each earlier round's defect with the right diagnosis.
+  ⚠ Two limits recorded rather than implied: it can only check relations whose ymls declare their
+  columns (staging under-declares — that produced a false positive that had to be removed), and it
+  does not cover the prose or seed surfaces.
+
+  ⭐ TWO THINGS `platform-reviewer` SETTLED IN PASSING, both worth keeping:
+    · The round-1 open LT05 question is CLOSED: `player_benchmark_metrics.sql`'s lengthened dict line
+      sits inside a `{% set %}` tag, which templates to nothing, so LT05 cannot see it. Not a defect.
+    · ⚠ **`_LEADERBOARD_METRICS` / `_LB_KEEP` in `export_site_data.py` are pinned by NO test** —
+      `tests/test_export_site_data.py` exercises `shape_leaderboards` with synthetic keys only. That
+      is pre-existing and systemic across every rename batch so far, not introduced here, and it
+      means a stale board key would ship silently. Worth its own issue.
+
+  ⭐ THE SEQUENCING QUESTION THIS RAISED, AND THE CPO'S ANSWER. Asked whether to build the
+  catalogue-to-calculation wiring (a context registry + a value-equivalence test, #91) BEFORE
+  finishing the renames, he chose **step 4 first, then the test** — on the reasoning that the test
+  compares values in models that have already built, so it cannot catch a broken reference, and that
+  building it now would mean writing column names and aliases that 34 renames are about to change.
+  ⚠ He also ruled MetricFlow **premature but the intended destination**: "I just wanted to make sure
+  that we can upgrade to semantic layer with MetricFlow once there is a use case... MetricFlow seems
+  to be an overkill for now. But I want to be prepared for it." Recorded so a later reader does not
+  re-open it: the catalogue stays machine-readable as the on-ramp, and nothing built now should have
+  to be undone to adopt it.
+
